  "id": "Sutton-DM2026_00121",
  "appeal_status": null,
  "appeal_start_date": null,
  "description": "Installation of an internally illuminated digital display and communications kiosk.",
  "development_type": "Other advertisements",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "The proposal, due to its excessive height and width, and excessively large advertisement digital displays, would visually dominate this section of the High Street in which the application site is located and would add to street clutter in this prominent, high-traffic location adjacent to a bus stop and sitting areas within the parade of cafes and shops. As such, the proposal would cause harm to the visual amenity and the character and appearance of the public realm within the Carshalton Village Conservation Area. The proposal is therefore contrary to aims and objectives of NPPF (para 141), Policies D4, D8 and T2 of the London Plan 2021, Policies 23, 28 and 30 of the Sutton Local Plan 2018 and Supplementary Planning Document 14 'Creating Locally Distinctive Places' and the Carshalton Village Conservation Area Character Appraisal and Management Plan (October, 2019).",
    "The proposed dual advertisement digital screens are unsuitable for this highly pedestrianised location near a busy bus stop, public seating, and cafe areas as the proposal would introduce a visual clutter and sensory stimulation that would harm the public realm and fail to protect pedestrian amenity. The proposal would introduce street furniture that would obstruct the footway and hinder bus stop access, in particular for people with mobility issues. As such, the proposal is contrary to Policies D8 and T2 of the London Plan 2021 and Policy 36 of the Sutton Local Plan 2018, and Sutton's Urban Design Guide 'Creating Locally Distinctive Places' SPD."
  ],
